# Code owners for the Tier 3 paths in docs/risk-tiers.md, and nothing else.
#
# The ruleset (.github/rulesets/main.json) sets require_code_owner_review, so a
# pull request that touches a path listed here and that someone other than the
# owner opened cannot merge until the owner approves it on GitHub. GitHub does
# not ask an author for their own review, so the owner's own pull requests,
# and anything opened with the owner's token, are not held (see
# docs/branch-protection.md). A pull request that touches none of these paths
# merges on the required check alone, as before.
#
# That is why there is no catch-all `*` line: it would put every other author's
# pull request behind the owner's approval. tests/test_codeowners.py fails if one comes back,
# or if this list and the area/safety-critical globs in .github/labeler.yml stop
# covering the same files. docs/branch-protection.md explains the rule and what
# it costs a sole maintainer.

# Every workflow, not only build.yml. Once a workflow is on main, any job in it
# can declare the production-signing environment and get the signing key, so a
# change to any of them from anyone but the owner waits for the owner.
# Renovate's pin bumps in workflows wait too; that is the cost.
/.github/workflows/                                           @Danathar

# The seven files AGENTS.md section 0 rule 2 names. The first, build.yml, is
# owned by the workflows line above.
/.github/actions/publish-native-image/                        @Danathar
/ci_tools/sign_image.py                                       @Danathar
/ci_tools/promote_stable.py                                   @Danathar
/ci_tools/check_akmods_cache.py                               @Danathar
/containerfiles/zfs-akmods/install_zfs_from_akmods_cache.py   @Danathar
/files/scripts/configure_signing_policy.py                    @Danathar

# The only local action the two signing jobs in build.yml run. It installs the
# cosign binary that receives the signing key, so it is owned like the key
# itself (#177, option B).
/.github/actions/install-signing-tools/                       @Danathar

# What the image installs onto every booted machine, the signing key, and the
# ZFS line and base-image values.
/files/                                                       @Danathar
/cosign.pub                                                   @Danathar
/ci/defaults.json                                             @Danathar

# What each workflow's token may do, what keeps main behind a pull request, and
# this file, which decides who must approve all of the above.
/.github/policies/workflow-permissions.json                   @Danathar
/.github/rulesets/                                            @Danathar
/.github/CODEOWNERS                                           @Danathar

# The agent permission boundary.
/.claude/settings.json                                        @Danathar
/.claude/hooks/                                               @Danathar
/.claude/commands/                                            @Danathar
/tests/run_tests.py                                           @Danathar
